milar, but probably at the cost of readability.\n\nWhat about the `countNeighbors` function? It takes a Cell and a Set<string>. The lookup pattern `liveSet.has(cellKey([...]))` creates a temporary array on every call. For performance, we could compute the key string directly without the intermediate array. But this would duplicate the key format, violating DRY.\n\nAlternatively, we could have `countNeighbors` take a key string directly, and compute neighbor keys by string manipulation. But that's ugly.\n\nOr we could change `cellKey` to take two numbers directly instead of a Cell tuple:\n\n```typescript\nfunction cellKey(x: number, y: number): string {\n  return `${x},${y}`;\n}\n```\n\nThis avoids creating temporary Cell arrays in `countNeighbors`. Let me see all the call sites:\n\n1. `const liveSet = new Set(cells.map(cellKey));` - Currently `cells.map(cellKey)` passes each Cell to cellKey. With the new signature, this would be `cells.map(([x, y]) => cellKey(x, y))`.\n\n2. `candidates.add(cellKey([cell[0] + dx, cell[1] + dy]));` → `candidates.add(cellKey(cell[0] + dx, cell[1] + dy));`\n\n3. `candidates.add(cellKey(cell));` → `candidates.add(cellKey(cell[0], cell[1]));`\n\n4. `countNeighbors` calls `cellKey([cell[0] + dx, cell[1] + dy])` → `cellKey(cell[0] + dx, cell[1] + dy)`\n\n5. `liveSet.has(key)` - unchanged\n\nHmm, call site 1 becomes more complex. Instead of `cells.map(cellKey)`, we'd need `cells.map(([x, y]) => cellKey(x, y))`. That's actually worse.\n\nWhat if we overload? No, TypeScript doesn't really support that well for this case.\n\nWhat if we keep `cellKey` taking a Cell but also have a `coordsKey(x, y)` function? That would add more elements (Rule 4 violation).\n\nOK, I think the most impactful single change is the rename `survives` → `willBeAlive`. Let me also remove the unnecessary early return. That gives us:\n\n1. Rename `survives` → `willBeAlive` (Rule 2: Reveals Intent)\n2. Remove `if (cells.length === 0) return [];` (Rule 4: Fewest Elements)\n\nLet me now implement these changes.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me run the tests to confirm they pass before refactoring:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9670c543eb89f9c1","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/zai-org/glm-5.1","usage":{"input":9746,"output":4864,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14610,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784966668053,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-0fc97cd7-e616-4d65-842e-12f9246f5bc6","responseModel":"zai-org/GLM-5.1"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-9670c543eb89f9c1","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_07-46-17_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_glm-5-1\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_07-46-17_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_glm-5-1\n\n ✓ src/game-of-life.spec.ts  (11 tests) 4ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  11 passed (11)\n   Start at  08:07:50\n   Duration  149ms (transform 25ms, setup 0ms, collect 22ms, tests 4ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784966870249}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":16248,"output":4912,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":14610,"turns":2},"model":"requesty/nebius/zai-org/glm-5.1","stopReason":"toolUse"}]}}}
